<title>PHILIPPINES: Jakarta gets $50 mln loan to upgrade water supply.</title>
<headline>Jakarta gets $50 mln loan to upgrade water supply.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Thursday it had approved a $50 million loan to help improve the water supply in Indonesian cities.</p>
<p>The loan is sourced from the bank's ordinary capital which carries an interest rate of 6.82 percent adjustable every six months, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>With the project, about half a million Indonesians will get better and safer supply of water, reducing the morbidity rate from waterborne diseases, it said.</p>
<p>The loan is repayable over 25 years with a five-year grace period.</p>
</text>
